                  "explanation": "Muscles produce force only as tension along their line of pull. That tension must be transmitted through tendons to bones, which act as levers rotating around joints. Without all three subsystems integrated, muscle force produces no useful movement.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quiz: System Integration</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Strong muscles alone do not lift heavy weight</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"190\" width=\"940\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">All Three Subsystems Required</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"305\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Muscle tension is useless without a lever to act on</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"345\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bone leverage is useless without a joint axis</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"385\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Joint motion is useless without muscular force</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"425\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tendon transmits — without it the chain breaks</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"490\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A 405 lb squat requires every link in working order</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"600\" width=\"940\" height=\"370\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why the Other Answers Fail</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"715\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">CNS connection enables firing — not biomechanical leverage</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"755\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Strong muscles plus weak tendons equals tendon rupture</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"795\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bones do not generate force — they only transmit it</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"860\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The integrated system answer is the only one supported</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"890\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">by basic biomechanics and applied physiology.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Force production needs muscle, tendon, bone, and joint working together."
                  }
