                {
                  "type": "quote",
                  "title": "Build Bone Like You Mean It",
                  "body": "\"You can't supplement your way out of an undertrained skeleton, and you can't train your way out of an underfed one. Strong bones in athletes come from heavy load applied consistently to a well-fed body over years. There are no shortcuts.\" The principles in this lesson — the remodeling cycle, RANK/RANKL/OPG signaling, Wolff's law, DEXA monitoring, stress fracture prevention, RED-S recognition — all integrate into one practical philosophy: respect the slow timeline of bone, but lean into the loading stimulus that drives it. Athletes who do this build skeletons that survive decades of training. Athletes who ignore it become statistics in the stress fracture literature.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Build Bone Like You Mean It</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Load it heavy, fuel it well, give it time</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"220\" width=\"940\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#888\" font-style=\"italic\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\"You can't supplement your way out of an</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"365\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#888\" font-style=\"italic\" text-anchor=\"middle\">undertrained skeleton, and you can't train your</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"410\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#888\" font-style=\"italic\" text-anchor=\"middle\">way out of an underfed one. Strong bones come</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"455\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#888\" font-style=\"italic\" text-anchor=\"middle\">from heavy load applied to a well-fed body</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#888\" font-style=\"italic\" text-anchor=\"middle\">over years. There are no shortcuts.\"</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"565\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">— Sports nutrition principle</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"630\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"690\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Integration: The Three Pillars</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"745\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Load: heavy lifts, impact work, multi-planar</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"785\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fuel: adequate calories, calcium, vitamin D, protein</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"825\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Time: months for adaptation, years for transformation</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"885\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">All three together equal lifelong skeletal strength</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Three pillars equal one resilient skeleton."
                  }
                }
